# Object Detection + Distance Estimation for Robotics Navigation

This assignment from Eric Robotics Pune is an end-to-end computer vision project. You are building a system that allows a robot to see navigation-relevant objects, recognize them, estimate how far away they are, and run the process efficiently on limited hardware.

The important part is that this is not just an object detection project. You need to combine three areas:

1\. Object detection

Detect traffic cones, barriers and stop signs in a camera image using a pretrained deep learning model.

2\. Distance estimation

Use camera calibration and geometric equations to estimate the distance from the camera to each detected object.

3\. Edge optimization

Reduce model size, memory use and inference latency while preserving acceptable detection and distance accuracy.

